{"event_id":"kimi-final-2:3","seq":3,"run_id":"kimi-final-2","session_id":"kimi-final-2","created_at":1789687189.555,"terminal":true,"type":"done","payload":{"status":"completed","last_seq":2,"result_summary":"approved: 3 finding(s)","review":{"schema_version":1,"verdict":"approved","risk":"read_only","markdown":"# Review\n\nApproved. The G25 host-only reopening slice validates action/admission/run identity and historical lease owner together, treats expired leases as inspection-only, binds exclusively to the exact canonical invocation journal (no Docker discovery, no worker receipts), enforces synchronous grants with digest rechecks across every await, rejects request/options mutation retargeting, and performs no start/replay/outcome inference/admission release. Adversarial tests cover substitution, journal tampering (digest/noncanonical/oversize/symlink/missing), grant revocation, stale fences, lost DELETE ACK, and real Linux daemon runs including a separate child process after SIGKILL of the original executor host, with held admission and unknown business state retained throughout. Remaining notes are informational only: concurrent stop is intentionally uncoalesced and untested as a race (conservative failure), and full OSStack Loop acceptance remains a separate pending gate.","judgments":[{"id":"ledger","pass":true,"severity":"error","summary":"inspectAdmission binds effect action, admission row, and historical lease owner in one fenced read; expired lease permits inspection only and is never stop proof; releasedAt!==null rejects reopening and no path releases held resources."},{"id":"binding","pass":true,"severity":"error","summary":"Reconstruction uses only the exact sha(invocationId) journal with bindingRef=sha(canonical data); candidate/command/digest/spec/daemon/generation/scope mismatches all throw CONTAINED_LEDGER_BINDING before any daemon call; no label search or worker receipt authority exists."},{"id":"authority","pass":true,"severity":"error","summary":"Synchronous current read/stop grants are enforced via authorize() (async return rejected), inputs are structuredClone-snapshotted pre-await, and recheck re-verifies admission digest and journal bytes across all awaits including executor operation callbacks; mutation-retarget tests confirm."},{"id":"unknown","pass":true,"severity":"error","summary":"Start is unconditionally rejected in recovery mode, no outcome inference or replay occurs, missing stop receipt and lost DELETE ACK leave the container unconfirmed and the business action unknown with admission held."},{"id":"tests","pass":true,"severity":"error","summary":"Tests drive real transitions (DB reopen, markUncertain, child-process reconstruction, real Linux daemon, SIGKILL probe) rather than asserting internals; substitution, journal tampering, grant revocation, and lost-ack adversarial cases are all exercised with deterministic passing evidence."}],"findings":[{"rule_id":"coverage.concurrent-stop","severity":"info","message":"Concurrent stop() is intentionally not coalesced and no test exercises two racing callers; a racing caller fails conservatively, which does not authorize release. Documented design choice, not a defect.","file":"packages/cli/src/graph-contained-recovery.ts","fingerprint":"a55abd699de0c9f53d33d6cd4f27dc8d61df0d97a656e581799621a066287305"},{"rule_id":"coverage.acceptance-gate","severity":"info","message":"Full OSStack Loop acceptance is still running and is a separate gate; this approval covers only the bounded G25 host-only reopening slice and its supplied evidence.","fingerprint":"948e2825de009271e1603983400a39cdf8fc155379702ef51b6b4a5dc4b3f03b"},{"rule_id":"coverage.trusted-test-grants","severity":"info","message":"Test fixtures use trusted noop read/stop grants as host wiring; these are not exposed as public authorization and do not weaken the sync-grant enforcement reviewed in production code.","fingerprint":"058e8943e893035bf6539beceb0cc6d705511f8a58e38e8e90a5d1706cb2abfd"}],"reco